# QRSeva Project Rules

You are working on QRSeva — an Indian restaurant QR ordering & management SaaS platform.

## MANDATORY: Read AGENTS.md before writing any code.
The file `AGENTS.md` in the project root contains the complete project context, architecture, conventions, and rules. Read it in full before making any changes.

## Quick Reference

- Domain: `qrseva.in` (NOT .com)
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite (separate app per surface)
- Backend: Firebase Cloud Functions (TypeScript)
- Database: Firestore (persistent) + Realtime Database (live orders/KDS)
- Hosting: Netlify (frontend), Firebase (backend)
- Currency: INR (₹), Indian market only

## Project Structure
- `sales-dashboard/` — Sales admin panel (sales.qrseva.in)
- `admin-dashboard/` — Restaurant admin panel (admin.qrseva.in)
- `customer-app/` — Customer ordering PWA (order.qrseva.in)
- `landing-page/` — Marketing website (qrseva.in)
- `packages/` — Shared UI, types, Firebase config, utils
- `functions/` — Firebase Cloud Functions
- `docs/` — All documentation (9 phases + deployment + SEO)

## Critical Rules
1. Each app is independent (separate package.json, vite.config.ts)
2. Customer ordering has NO login — guest checkout only
3. Restaurant self-signup creates PENDING account — sales must approve
4. Use @qrseva/shared-types for all TypeScript interfaces
5. Validate all Cloud Function inputs with Zod
6. All data access is tenant-isolated (filter by restaurantId)
7. Plan-gate premium features using PlanGate component
8. Audit log all sensitive operations

## Documentation
Read phase docs in `docs/` folder for detailed specifications:
- Phase 0: Architecture | Phase 1: Data Models | Phase 2: Auth & Sales
- Phase 3: Admin Dashboard | Phase 4: Customer Ordering | Phase 5: KDS
- Phase 6: Billing | Phase 7: Reports | Phase 8: Landing Page | Phase 9: Security
